{"beat": 38, "name": "THE STEP", "text": "So how do you step when you can't see the top? Work the formula at the estimate alone. If that puts the best price above today's, step up: near minus one the top runs off to the right, and the estimate agrees. If it puts it below today's while the range still reaches minus one, hold: the estimate says down, and the range can't rule out far up. And never by much: the demo's model caps any single move at 5%, so that a wrong step costs little and a right one shows up in the data. A small step you can measure beats a confident number you can't. And sometimes the right step is none at all.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "So", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.16}, {"word": "how", "start": 0.16, "end": 0.34}, {"word": "do", "start": 0.34, "end": 0.46}, {"word": "you", "start": 0.46, "end": 0.56}, {"word": "step", "start": 0.56, "end": 0.84}, {"word": "when", "start": 0.84, "end": 1.06}, {"word": "you", "start": 1.06, "end": 1.18}, {"word": "can't", "start": 1.18, "end": 1.52}, {"word": "see", "start": 1.52, "end": 1.64}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.64, "end": 1.78}, {"word": "top?", "start": 1.78, "end": 2.08}, {"word": "Work", "start": 2.6, "end": 2.8}, {"word": "the", "start": 2.8, "end": 3.0}, {"word": "formula", "start": 3.0, "end": 3.46}, {"word": "at", "start": 3.46, "end": 3.72}, {"word": "the", "start": 3.72, "end": 3.82}, {"word": "estimate", "start": 3.82, "end": 4.18}, {"word": "alone.", "start": 4.18, "end": 4.54}, {"word": "If", "start": 5.32, "end": 5.46}, {"word": "that", "start": 5.46, "end": 5.66}, {"word": "puts", "start": 5.66, "end": 5.86}, {"word": "the", "start": 5.86, "end": 6.1}, {"word": "best", "start": 6.1, "end": 6.38}, {"word": "price", "start": 6.38, "end": 6.74}, {"word": "above", "start": 6.74, "end": 6.98}, {"word": "today's,", "start": 6.98, "end": 7.7}, {"word": "step", "start": 7.8, "end": 8.02}, {"word": "up:", "start": 8.02, "end": 8.28}, {"word": "near", "start": 8.86, "end": 9.06}, {"wo